**Certification (paras 7, 59, 60):** banks identify specialised areas and make a **certificate course mandatory before posting** in at least:
- treasury (dealers, mid-office);
- risk management (credit, market, operational, enterprise-wide, information security, liquidity);
- accounting (financial results, audit function);
- credit management (appraisal, rating, monitoring, administration);
- marketing third-party retail and wealth products, where other regulators' certifications also apply.

Relevant university degrees, diplomas and certificates may count. Banks choose suitable courses from those **recognised by IBA** and set them in a **Board-approved policy** (approval can be delegated to a Board committee).

**Mandatory leave (paras 61-63B):** staff in **sensitive positions** must take leave of **at least 10 working days in one spell each year**, **without prior notice**, and lose access to work systems (except general email) while away. Banks also need a **staff rotation** policy. Internal and concurrent auditors check both and examine the decisions of anyone not rotated or not sent on leave.
